 ## Overview
-Outline and Contour Generation is a family of non-photorealistic volume rendering techniques that enhance perceptual clarity by explicitly detecting and rendering edges, silhouettes, or topological boundaries within volumetric data [S2, unofficial][S1, unofficial]. Unlike surface-based NPR, which relies on well-defined geometric surfaces, this family operates on continuous volumetric fields where feature areas must be determined through local property analysis [S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Line Illustration Detection](772-line-illustration-detection.md) by focusing on boundary emphasis and structural outlines rather than flow-aligned strokes, and from [LOG-based Silhouette Detection](6322-log-based-silhouette-detection.md) by employing diverse detection mechanisms ranging from gradient-based particle tracing to user-defined interactive selection [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+Outline and Contour Generation is a family of non-photorealistic volume rendering techniques that enhance perceptual clarity by extracting and stylizing significant edges, such as silhouettes, feature lines, and topological boundaries, from volumetric data [S2, unofficial][S1, unofficial]. Unlike surface-based NPR, which relies on well-defined geometric surfaces, this family operates on continuous volumetric fields by identifying feature areas through local volumetric properties like gradients and normals [S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Line Illustration Detection](772-line-illustration-detection.md) by focusing on boundary emphasis and structural outlines rather than flow-aligned strokes, and from [LOG-based Silhouette Detection](6322-log-based-silhouette-detection.md) by offering a broader range of contour types including topological landscapes and user-defined selections.
 
