-### Image Space Outline Generation
-#### definition
-- [S1, unofficial] A pixel-based method to generate simple outlines by extracting edges from depth or normal maps, observing that depth differences are minimal between adjacent pixels of a single object and large between objects, and normals vary smoothly across a single surface but show discontinuity between surfaces.
-#### step
-- [S1, unofficial] Extract edges from a depth map or normal map using an edge detection mechanism, such as the Sobel filter.
-- [S1, unofficial] Combine detected depth and normal edges to yield perceptually significant silhouettes.
-- [S1, unofficial] For further processing (e.g., modifying line qualities), calculate analytical curves from the detected edge map, as detected edges only exist as lists of pixels.
-#### comparison
-- [S1, unofficial] Depth edges reflect C0 discontinuities, while normal edges reflect C1 discontinuities; combining both yields all perceptually significant silhouettes.
+#### Image Space Outline Generation
+**Definition**
+A pixel-based method to generate simple outlines by extracting edges from depth or normal maps, observing that depth differences are minimal between adjacent pixels of a single object and large between objects, and normals vary smoothly across a single surface but show discontinuity between surfaces [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Steps**
+1.  Extract edges from a depth map or normal map using an edge detection mechanism, such as the Sobel filter [S1, unofficial].
+2.  Combine detected depth and normal edges to yield perceptually significant silhouettes [S1, unofficial].
+3.  For further processing (e.g., modifying line qualities), calculate analytical curves from the detected edge map, as detected edges only exist as lists of pixels [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Comparison**
+Depth edges reflect C0 discontinuities, while normal edges reflect C1 discontinuities; combining both yields all perceptually significant silhouettes [S1, unofficial].
 
